From 386e9e2ca130b0461b3eff4f6e3750267d229613 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nst <49988403+nenas1ya@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 12:38:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(profiles): send custom request headers with subscription
 updates

A URL profile now carries a map of HTTP headers that is sent with every
download of its subscription, for panels that only answer clients
identifying themselves, such as a Remnawave device limit expecting
x-hwid. Nothing is sent unless the user adds a header.

Credentials in the URL still become the Authorization header, and a
User-Agent among the headers replaces the client one. The editor only
accepts names and values dart:io can send, and Content-Length and
Transfer-Encoding are dropped since a GET has no body to frame.

Changelog: Per-profile custom headers for subscription requests
